# a-wall-against-a-scout — plan 23 K0.
#
# The twin of `a-wall-against-a-miner.keys`, one word different:
# `wave 1 miner` is `wave 1 scout`.  Same corridor, same 15 HP stub,
# same nine ticks of walking — and after three ticks of siege the
# wall reads 14.7-14.9 HP where the miner left it at 9.0.
#
# ⚠ **Read the two together or neither means anything.**  A single
# scout chewing slowly is not evidence of a per-class rate; a scout
# and a miner doing measurably different things to the SAME wall is.
# That is `docs/DESIGN.md` § Small robots as a pair of runs.
#
# ── What the long tick count is for ─────────────────────────────
#
# The last reading ticks thirty more and the wall is STILL standing at
# roughly 12.9 — which is the phase's real claim.  `a-wall-breaks.keys`
# establishes that one robot opens this stub in twenty-three ticks of
# siege; a scout has done less than a sixth of that job in forty.
#
# ⚠ It is not zero, and that is deliberate rather than a rounding
# artefact.  A class that did NOTHING would drop out of `wave_damage`
# entirely and stop being counted in `count targets` — the HUD would
# tell a player nothing was happening to a wall an enemy was standing
# on, which is false.  `count targets 1 1` below is that property.
#
# ── The world (identical to its twin) ───────────────────────────
#
#   one corridor of grass, twelve hexes:  (12, 0) -> (0, 0)
#   sealed at (2, 0) with a wall          15 HP — a STUB, unbraced
#   core at (0, 0), spawn at (12, 0)

echo a wall against a scout: 0.1 HP/s, and the seal holds

do toggle_mode

# The core is where the target is.
do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

# The spawn, twelve hexes out — clear of close_spawn_disable_radius
# (10) and inside the scrambler bubble (25).
# ⚠ TWICE: the place-kind cycle is spawn -> target -> tower -> spawn
# since plan 12 B5a gave towers a marker kind of their own.
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 12 0
marker 12 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag 12 0 0 0
count painted 13 13

palette 9
click 2 0
kind 2 0 wall
count painted 13 13

wave 1 scout
count alive 1 1
count targets 0 0
hp 2 0 15.0 15.0

# The pre-walk window (plan 16 W2): 8 ticks standing at the marker.
tick 8
enemy 0 12 0
hp 2 0 15.0 15.0

# Nine ticks to arrive at (3, 0), untouched wall — the same reading
# its twin takes, and the last one the two files agree on.
tick 9
enemy 0 3 0
enemies passable
count targets 1 1
target 0 2 0
hp 2 0 15.0 15.0

# ── Three ticks of siege — the comparison ───────────────────────
#
# 3 x per_tick(0.1) = 0.2 HP.  The miner took 6.0 in the same three
# ticks: THIRTY times the bite, on the same hex, from a robot the
# mover cannot tell apart.
tick 3
hp 2 0 14.7 14.9
enemy 0 3 0

# ── Thirty more, and it is still a wall ─────────────────────────
#
# 30 x per_tick(0.1) = 2.0 more.  Forty ticks of siege have taken a
# seventh of a stub that a single ROBOT opens in twenty-three, and
# the scout is standing where the miner had already walked through.
#
# ⚠ `count targets 1 1` is the half of this that is not about the
# number: it is still besieging, and the game still says so.
tick 30
kind 2 0 wall
hp 2 0 12.7 12.9
enemy 0 3 0
count targets 1 1
target 0 2 0

snap k0-the-scout-at-the-wall
